[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37084"] :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & a \\\\ 3 & b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $D={P}^{-1}AP,$ find the value of $\\frac{b}{a}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagonal matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$, we deduce that the eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3.$\n\nSo, the second column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=3.$ \n\nNow, we simply need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{2}=3.$ Computing $A-3I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-3I & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]-(3)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=2,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{2}{1}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186124947 :question/answer-fields 17592186122704] {:db/id "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/d3f6a4997de3203608004e887f7c08b27f73a81e8223182d9d980d2445815b32" :answer/id #uuid "80fc5203-e5b3-5c36-938e-31a62fad77fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/5280493cb371bf80683ddea293701d43d5e6bcfbb3ff8bc4bad8b7cdd03d633c" :answer/id #uuid "c5e62b23-8dc9-56d1-bac4-d21592e96c4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/fde7c7e8c5c0e1280c4619c1897573fc8396a25055092e595f0052889d677717" :answer/id #uuid "cc0d7ffc-d6f1-53ad-a001-f38b4573bd86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ is not diagonalizable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/c9556f887b26b159da22acb2e1850fa3deff53e8543cdd7d28ba29c4da40a8c7" :answer/id #uuid "74009c24-373b-5401-a54c-29a58e4bfddb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/0acfa149c590eae0d2f7d0aa2345604a38891d0184c71d8fa371bbb6bc3eadd7" :answer/id #uuid "e3165b87-1939-5359-813a-63c4d669a625" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d89e01c-bdb6-5d2f-a589-4e0a25f7730e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/d3f6a4997de3203608004e887f7c08b27f73a81e8223182d9d980d2445815b32" :answer-field/choices ["q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/d3f6a4997de3203608004e887f7c08b27f73a81e8223182d9d980d2445815b32" "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/5280493cb371bf80683ddea293701d43d5e6bcfbb3ff8bc4bad8b7cdd03d633c" "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/fde7c7e8c5c0e1280c4619c1897573fc8396a25055092e595f0052889d677717" "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/c9556f887b26b159da22acb2e1850fa3deff53e8543cdd7d28ba29c4da40a8c7" "q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba/0acfa149c590eae0d2f7d0aa2345604a38891d0184c71d8fa371bbb6bc3eadd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37086"] :question/problem "Given the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$, \nfind a diagonal matrix $D$ and an invertible matrix $P$ such that $D={P}^{-1}AP.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.**  We need to find the eigenvalues of the matrix. Since matrix $A$ is triangular, its eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal: \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=3$\n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]-(-1)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $2$nd one). Thus, ${x}_{1}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=0.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=1,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-3I & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a homogeneous system of linear equations with the matrix as above. Note, the matrix is already in row echelon form. There is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=2,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37086/selection/ma-v1/8e8edcdd53478fa62284af5dbda477db6b89f159e0d6914e6a0a53978109f4ba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-140038/selection/eaf2e27ddf87ca63e89fb7e23bf1588375cefb40ce26550d618d421a29470359" :answer/id #uuid "d1463024-3b5f-5108-8daa-d59f2b489ae7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140038/selection/c8769bb8df24138ca302a8deafeabc80683dc50a472a659edcb37316f21e0d7f" :answer/id #uuid "b5ca9a41-0a4c-5a58-8839-896f24c8988f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140038/selection/ee144ac56c0276681b3a91f07710905727aca897ae0079381eab14029c30dd56" :answer/id #uuid "3e416a00-c3fa-54e3-81f2-0d654ae7084e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140038/selection/102b4336766af3d2869aaf451989b1163af51df0908b6c3ac20000e09a16f4ad" :answer/id #uuid "961bae0e-7819-512a-89ab-e9168684277f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140038/selection/19cc36fb71702bc73d59360a04f34ecc8984aa553112be9d3cf6d23bbb77031d" :answer/id #uuid "324f9ee4-75b5-55db-a322-0eba9f63ca87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140038/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d1135ba-2178-5e51-adef-36de78675659" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140038/selection/eaf2e27ddf87ca63e89fb7e23bf1588375cefb40ce26550d618d421a29470359" :answer-field/choices ["q-140038/selection/eaf2e27ddf87ca63e89fb7e23bf1588375cefb40ce26550d618d421a29470359" "q-140038/selection/c8769bb8df24138ca302a8deafeabc80683dc50a472a659edcb37316f21e0d7f" "q-140038/selection/ee144ac56c0276681b3a91f07710905727aca897ae0079381eab14029c30dd56" "q-140038/selection/102b4336766af3d2869aaf451989b1163af51df0908b6c3ac20000e09a16f4ad" "q-140038/selection/19cc36fb71702bc73d59360a04f34ecc8984aa553112be9d3cf6d23bbb77031d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140038" :question/id #uuid "152de614-310b-5169-9d3a-b26f9bc07c9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140038" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -8 \\\\ 12 & -9\\end{aligned}].$ You're given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3$ are the eigenvalues of $A$, and\n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are the respective eigenvectors. Find the matrices $P$ and $D$ such that $PD{P}^{-1}=A,$ where $D$ is a diagonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=3.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140038/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5164c6cb-aef0-554b-b361-77245991c0ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140054/selection/de358ebcf6ff79d7a7c5ad936e6ace1eff03ecf3ee0c86ee7ef2330b40f42cb4" :answer/id #uuid "375a4cdb-76a8-5628-9c53-8c4ffa4b1f04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140054/selection/09779989549eddae9a4670ff8e91f68253604123a40485704e62c03fb3a5a18f" :answer/id #uuid "d75681f1-763e-5b03-8ec5-8f8830cde0af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140054/selection/2caf8873a0b6230d1da4479e09489513e971f6209e4cc0bf9afd97773ef077b2" :answer/id #uuid "10238492-9ba6-5fcb-b5c1-db4cfe35efff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ is not diagonalizable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140054/selection/144b3ef0fd2ba105076940e98a4d3dd73d10afc225e2a4520732d7a8a7817539" :answer/id #uuid "11090dd0-640a-5b19-8e06-36e0459a8700" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140054/selection/7ece4088ad25498ec38d277432f4cc177f16548bf0467b7d1b845defcfbfbf79" :answer/id #uuid "0fedfd3a-33f6-5bfe-b008-025a0b87b5e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140054/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "309bdeaf-c149-5563-ac66-010f83b3bc19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140054/selection/7ece4088ad25498ec38d277432f4cc177f16548bf0467b7d1b845defcfbfbf79" :answer-field/choices ["q-140054/selection/de358ebcf6ff79d7a7c5ad936e6ace1eff03ecf3ee0c86ee7ef2330b40f42cb4" "q-140054/selection/09779989549eddae9a4670ff8e91f68253604123a40485704e62c03fb3a5a18f" "q-140054/selection/2caf8873a0b6230d1da4479e09489513e971f6209e4cc0bf9afd97773ef077b2" "q-140054/selection/144b3ef0fd2ba105076940e98a4d3dd73d10afc225e2a4520732d7a8a7817539" "q-140054/selection/7ece4088ad25498ec38d277432f4cc177f16548bf0467b7d1b845defcfbfbf79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140054" :question/id #uuid "c8ba5efd-df6b-5909-aa3d-810a6e4be2f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-140054" :question/problem "Find matrices $P$ and $D$ such that $PD{P}^{-1}=B,$ where $D$ is a diagonal matrix and $B=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.** We need to find the eigenvalues of the matrix $B$ using its characteristic equation $det(B-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & -6 \\\\ 8 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )-(-6)\\cdot 8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-49+48 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $B$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1.$\n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $B.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -7\\end{aligned}]-(-1)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=4,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-1I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -7\\end{aligned}]-1[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{4}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-140054/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ff6446e-7913-5d55-adfd-124649f3f1c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
